commit 8c3186edfdcab4415f0adcced4c55d0a7e638459

C03: a control that disappears after a verified click is not a disabled control (UI1637)

UI1635 measured that a reviewed input.visible.click on the Aceptar button of a root-authored dialog completes and verifies — the dialog closes — while two finals narrated the receipt's post-read (absentOrDisabled: the control was gone after the click) as a failure («el control estaba deshabilitado», «not clickable because it was absent or disabled»). The click receipt is now projected to the composer as the click done and the control gone afterwards (its dialog or view closed), and a verified click narrated as disabled, unclickable or not found is vetoed as reversed_result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


